==English==
[[File:Topped lavender.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lavendre}}, from {{der|en|xno|lavendre|}} ({{cog|fr|lavande}}), from {{der|en|ML.|lavendula}}, possibly from {{der|en|la|lividus||bluish}}, but influenced by {{m|la|lavō|t=wash}} due to use of lavender in washing clothes.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlæv.ən.də/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lavender.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlæv.ən.dɚ/|a=GA}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q171892}}Any of a group of European [[plant]]s, genus, {{taxfmt|Lavandula|genus}}, of the [[mint]] family.
# A [[pale]] [[bluish]] [[purple]] [[color|colour]], like that of the lavender flower.
#: {{color panel|957EDC}}
#: {{color panel|web lavender|E6E6FA}}
# {{lb|en|film|historical|uncountable}} A kind of [[film stock]] for creating [[positive]] [[print]]s from [[negative]]s as part of the process of duplicating the negatives.

